  (text "J1 castellated edge: 1.0 mm half-holes on a 0.1 in grid, three per edge.\nViewed from the top with the antenna at the bottom, pads count\ncounter-clockwise from the top-left. All I/O is 3.3 V.\n1 GND (left edge)\n2 UART_TX: PB13, module out (left edge)\n3 UART_RX: PB12, module in (left edge)\n4 NRST: not connected (right edge)\n5 VCC in, 3.3 to 6.0 V (right edge)\n6 GND (right edge)\n7 SWDIO: PB14 (top edge)\n8 SWCLK: PB15, also the ROM ISP strap (top edge)\n9 WAKE: PA11, module out (top edge)"
    (at 195.58 93.98 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "2e41c537-e15a-4637-95e4-6bc62ebdc061")
  )
  (text "PB15 low at power-on puts the CH592D in ROM ISP. The boot ROM pulls PB15 up,\nso leave J1 pad 8 open or high at power-up. A blank part programs over SWD (pads 7 and 8)."
    (at 167.64 160.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "4d68d68d-b687-43c5-a884-3264b835e555")
  )
  (text "U2 feeds VIO33/VDD33 (pin 5). C2 2.2 uF sits at pin 5 and is also the LDO output capacitor.\nDC-DC: VSW (pin 4) drives L1 10 uH into VDCID (pin 3), decoupled by C4 4.7 uF; VDCIA (pin 16) is tied to VDCID.\nThe DC-DC is off at power-on (VSW then passes VDD33 through L1); firmware enables it. C5 470 nF decouples VINTA (pin 14).\nY1 has no external load capacitors: the CH592 provides programmable internal load capacitance.\nANT (pin 15) drives the PCB antenna directly, as on OpenDongle.\nThe CH592D has no reset pin, so J1 pad 4 (NRST) is not connected. USB (PB10/PB11) is not brought out."
    (at 101.6 110.49 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "dc191b3b-100d-4395-bf3a-6450912c39ac")
  )
